[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714305623","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114582#issuecomment-3714305623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114582","id":3714305623,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dY85X","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T11:12:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T11:18:04Z","body":"> adding a button like \"Open AnimationLibraryManager\" to the Inspector might be feasible\r\n\r\nI would prefer this. Inspector buttons are now easy to add by defining a non-storage (`PROPERTY_USAGE_EDITOR`) property with hing `PROPERTY_HINT_TOOL_BUTTON` and type `Variant::CALLABLE` \r\n\r\nIt should be possible to bind this callable to a private member function `#if TOOLS_ENABLED` that can check if editor and invoke a function on the editor to open the animation library editor.\r\n\r\nRight now, it is possible to save animation libraries from the inspector by right clicking the resource or swap libraries. I have used this before to quickly save a library from an imported scene without going through the animation panel. Having a button would be the best.\r\n\r\n(Also, I'd like at some point to be able to edit an AnimationLibrary resource as well, without needing to add it to a node, but that's a separate problem.)\r\n\r\n\r\nedit: the annoying thing about tool_button is you need to add a case to the `_get` function to check for some builtin property name string like `_open_library_editor` and return the callable, or else expose a underscore / private function to the api that returns a function to open an editor, but I don't know if this affects compatibility. Ideally it would not be part of the official API.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714305623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3746636694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114582#issuecomment-3746636694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114582","id":3746636694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fUSOW","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","